title: BabushkaDialogue
---

<<if DoesHeKnow("BABASetting")>>	
	(Enter BABUSHKA)
<<else>>
	<<Learn BABASetting>>
	SETTING - Beneath a dim streetlight in the River District. Next to a well.

	AT RISE - A weary dame, known to all the younger generation as BABA, notices SASHA's approach.

	NARRATOR: Clutching in her wrinkled hands, a matryoshka grieving doll that is cherished by all those who have lost one dear.
	NARRATOR: But Baba sitting alone like this-- she's not only lost a loved one.
	<< Learn BabushkaTarot >>
	<< Learn BabushkaInfoA >> // The Grandmother of the town.

	<< if $PsychMajor == true >>
		PSY: Even with that puppy-dog sadness, she has some relief in that blind gaze of hers.
	<< elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
		ART: Whoever is in the urn wasn't native to Solster. Only those born here have their urns painted in their semblance, and this one looks like a typical Matryoshka doll.
		ART: The paint looks barely dry, and not to mention shaky.. she must have barely gotten it done in time for the parade.
	<< elseif $TechMajor == true >>
		TECH: The craftsmanship of that doll is almost shabby. Surely no one made her make it herself?
	<< endif >>

	BABA: (silence)
	SASHA: ...
	BABA: ...
	BABA: (sudden gasp, looks at SASHA)
	BABA: Oh! Bless mothers threads. Hello there, child.
	BABA: It is not often mother blesses us with visitors from outside the void.
	BABA: (a little mellower) And on the day of the parade, nonetheless! 
	BABA: Oh! How incredibly wonderful!
	BABA: It has been years since we have had someone from outside of Solster join the parade.
	BABA: (gazes down at the doll) How incredibly wonderful, and today of all days..

	-> “Well, I was actually born here in Solster.”
		Sasha: “Well, I was actually born here in Solster.”
	-> Say nothing
		Sasha: (Say nothing.)

	BABA: (continuing, as if not realized) Most people around here won't be as kind to an outsider like you 
	BABA: An odd thing really, I have never understood. Our most cherished things come from the outside.
	BABA: Without brave Dynnra we would have never learned the power of the void.
	BABA: Without the radiant Elegy and the Everwatcher we would be lost in the dark, we would have no power, and no one to look up to for protection.

	-> “Yes, I understand, but I’m from Solster--”
		Sasha: “Yes, I understand, but I’m from Solster--”
	-> Say nothing and accept the situation.

	BABA: (intenser, offended at the thought you would be supposedly discriminated against) Who knows, maybe you will be the next outsider to make a difference. 
	BABA: Since you are new here, many things must still be confusing to you.
	BABA: If you have any questions about Solster and its customs, I will be here for you, child.
	BABA: Don't be afraid to ask something, anything.
	BABA: It can get a bit lonely sometimes, haha.. (slow, slightly pained)

	NARRATOR: It was hard to recognise her at first with her discolored, marbling and plastic looking skin. Her nose seems sharper and her eyes and cheeks are sunken in. 
	NARRATOR: But behind all of that sits a woman who would always give out bandaids and quick prayers to the kids who scraped their knees while playing. 
	NARRATOR: The woman who would watch over them while their parents worked hard to put food on the table. 
	NARRATOR: The woman whose freshly baked pastries would sit in the window sill, spreading a sweet smell of cinnamon, vanilla and roasted nuts throughout the streets of the River District.

	BABA: Oh, but I do make sure to catch the parade today, so let’s not get too carried away with chatting.
	BABA: It is quite a sight to behold I tell you. 
	BABA: (silence)
	<< if $PsychMajor == true >>
		PSY: The silence is almost overwhelming. Was it always this quiet in the district? It's as if she notices too.
	<< elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
		ART: In this moment you can look through the district and its.. decrepitness. Was it always this run down?
	<< elseif $TechMajor == true >>
		TECH: The lamplight above her is flickering almost dangerously. Someone should get that checked out, before the darkness consumes this area.
	<< endif >>

	BABA: (slight pause, gasp) Oh mother, forgive me, I almost forgot! The name is Maacah, …. but please just call me Babushka.

	-> "Nice to meet you. My name is Sasha"
	-> "I'm pretty sure you already know me."

	<< if $PsychMajor == true >>
		PSY: It feels bad to do this, but you only have so much time before the parade. You leave, with her barely noticing.
	<< elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
		ART: It feels bad to do this, but you only have so much time before the parade. You leave, with her barely noticing.
	<< elseif $TechMajor == true >>
		TECH: It feels bad to do this, but you only have so much time before the parade. You leave, with her barely noticing.
	<< endif >>
	<<stop>>
<<endif>>

BABA: (hopeful) Yes..?

-> "Just checking up on you."
-> Sit by her side for a moment.


===
